      "html" : "<\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-193064\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-193064\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>Components of the condensate disposal system shall be cast iron, galvanized steel, copper, cross-linked polyethylene, polyethylene, ABS, CPVC, or PVC pipe or tubing. Polypropylene tubing may be used in lengths that do not exceed 12 inches (304.8 mm) for an individual drain application. Components shall be selected for the pressure and temperature rating of the installation. Joints and connections shall be made in accordance with the applicable provisions of <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-162437', hash: '#JD_PCCh.7' }}\">Chapter 7<\/Link> of the <span style=\"font-weight: normal;font-style: italic;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">New York City Plumbing Code<\/span> relative to the material type. Condensate waste and drain line size shall be not less than 3\/4-inch (19.1 mm) internal diameter and shall not decrease in size from the drain pan connection to the place of condensate disposal. Where the drain pipes from more than one unit are manifolded together for condensate drainage, the pipe or tubing shall be sized in accordance with <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-193063', hash: '#JD_MCTable307.2.2' }}\">Table 307.2.2<\/Link>.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-193065\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-193065\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><a name=\"JD_MCTable307.2.2\" id=\"JD_MCTable307.2.2\" title=\"MC Table 307.2.2\"><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Table 307.2.2<br><\/br>Condensate Drain Sizing<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-193066\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-193066\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<div class=\"xsl-table\">",
      "id" : "10292-html-1",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "Components of the condensate disposal system shall be cast iron, galvanized steel, copper, cross-linked polyethylene, polyethylene, ABS, CPVC, or PVC pipe or tubing. Polypropylene tubing may be used in lengths that do not exceed 12 inches (304.8 mm) for an individual drain application. Components shall be selected for the pressure and temperature rating of the installation. Joints and connections shall be made in accordance with the applicable provisions of Chapter 7 of the New York City Plumbing Code relative to the material type. Condensate waste and drain line size shall be not less than 3\/4-inch (19.1 mm) internal diameter and shall not decrease in size from the drain pan connection to the place of condensate disposal. Where the drain pipes from more than one unit are manifolded together for condensate drainage, the pipe or tubing shall be sized in accordance with Table 307.2.2 .\n\n Table 307.2.2\n Condensate Drain Sizing"
    },
